The Wise One is the elite class of the Hedge Witch (good witch route). It
needs alignment +30 or higher at level 30. Its hexes ward the company as they
land, and its wards give more than protection.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Hearthward       a landed hex wards the three most hurt allies, each ward
                      absorbing up to 2 average hits
  35 Deep Slumber     Slumber lasts another round (a foe is still never asleep
                      more than half a fight)
  40 Mend Charm       when one of its wards breaks, the warded ally heals
                      half of a Minor Heal
  45 Cleansing ward   a breaking ward also removes one harmful status
  50 Hearth's Peace   allies holding its ward have +5 Evasion
  55 Wider Hearthward a landed hex wards the four most hurt allies
  60 Ward of Life     once a battle, a warded ally who would fall stays at 1
                      health

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

The Wise One hexes on its own like any witch (<ansi fg="command">help witch</ansi>). Each hex that
lands wards the most hurt allies who have no ward yet; the line names who. A
ward absorbs a number of blows, up to its cap each, and its gifts end with it.
A ward is not renewed while it stands.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Witch elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves (+10% maximum mana),
Iron Will (blows break your chant 25% less often), Hex Reach (+5 to a hex's
chance to land). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help witch-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
